cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: situs
abstract: >-
  Spatial indexes over f64 boxes in Rust, with no false negatives. The crate
  provides a static R-tree bulk-loaded by Sort-Tile-Recursive packing and a
  dynamic R*-tree with insertion and exact removal, both answering box
  queries, a dual-tree join and nearest-neighbor search. Box queries return
  exactly the entries whose boxes meet the window. Nearest-neighbor search
  ranks candidates by f64 bounds on each squared distance that are proven to
  bracket the exact value, so rounding can add candidates but never remove
  one, and no distance is presented as exact. Under the optional
  exact-nearest feature, candidates are ranked exactly with arithmetica. The
  crate is no_std with alloc and has no dependencies by default.
